{"id": "EUVD-2026-59339", "enisaUuid": "523e25ae-a9a5-35e9-9df1-905c3475b188", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid1: fix writes_pending and barrier reference leaks on write failures\n\nraid1_make_request() acquires a writes_pending reference with\nmd_write_start() before calling raid1_write_request(). Several failure\npaths in raid1_write_request() complete the bio and return without\nreaching the normal write completion path, causing the corresponding\nmd_write_end() to be skipped.\n\nMake raid1_write_request() return a status indicating whether the write\nrequest was successfully queued. This allows raid1_make_request() to\ncall md_write_end() when raid1_write_request() fails.\n\nAdditionally, if wait_blocked_rdev() fails after wait_barrier()\nsucceeds, the associated barrier reference is not released.\n\nCall allow_barrier() before returning from that path to keep the barrier\naccounting balanced.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:57", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/921e2baa626d1504bf30295816aaeb90ac8c82f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a846affa813013204d0cce0cfdaeb99e8fcce188", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a450460687919e79b5f8503bdeb13ecf4cca311", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bffbbfcbd9393e315a7a4286dcd70e875265db9a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e065a1602511282fc0da2dc89445e0eb71a681c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jh9h-wfxq-pfm4", "CVE-2026-72440"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10bf8726-6d79-3130-afd7-1feaa49702fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.17"}, {"id": "3552c948-c596-3ee1-9a75-12d3d7eb57ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "36e7d6dc-2e0b-3de3-8d1e-3f4c6888a60d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "6916fbc0-a4f3-300f-af1a-d6b973b39466", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6fe71bb4-66f6-329c-a520-e424db349949", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "8e5172ac-76e1-3b83-93f5-8dd027274114", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "9fcdbd6c-0b33-3cd9-94ae-9f8eb45bf71f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5aa705039c4fca84575539bfa2b8a28454a3d2ca <a846affa813013204d0cce0cfdaeb99e8fcce188"}, {"id": "c616365e-5371-3326-b021-e2268930bd20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5aa705039c4fca84575539bfa2b8a28454a3d2ca <921e2baa626d1504bf30295816aaeb90ac8c82f4"}, {"id": "d1cf9dba-7e8b-3550-ab36-e43dad9434f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5aa705039c4fca84575539bfa2b8a28454a3d2ca <bffbbfcbd9393e315a7a4286dcd70e875265db9a"}, {"id": "d707e357-c556-3a46-906d-640f677920ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5aa705039c4fca84575539bfa2b8a28454a3d2ca <8e065a1602511282fc0da2dc89445e0eb71a681c"}, {"id": "da678734-0bf5-3e19-8883-fe4cc5bc5640", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5aa705039c4fca84575539bfa2b8a28454a3d2ca <7a450460687919e79b5f8503bdeb13ecf4cca311"}, {"id": "e0dc332b-7aea-3bae-a7f1-a12c2a655cc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a8e5e655-2d99-35c0-8274-b37ca8e22650", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}